  <name>Monad</name>
  <summary>Mine Monero with a minimal interface</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.numbpill3d">
    <name>numbpill3d</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Monad is a minimalist Monero (XMR) miner. Paste your wallet address,
      press Start, and watch the hashrate. It uses the XMRig RandomX engine
      on your CPU and works with any Stratum pool.
    </p>
    <p>Developer fee: 2% of hashing time (about one minute in every fifty) is
      mined to the developer's wallet on pool.supportxmr.com to fund
      development. The status line shows “Developer fee” while it runs. Time
      is only counted while actually hashing. XMRig's own donation is disabled,
      so the total fee is 2%.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>One-click start and stop, nothing runs in the background</li>
      <li>Validates Monero addresses before mining</li>
      <li>Adjustable CPU usage</li>
      <li>TLS pool connections</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Mining uses a lot of electricity and makes your CPU run hot. Only mine on hardware you own or are allowed to use.</p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.numbpill3d.Monad.desktop</launchable>
